{"parentUuid":"0603d0d7-1e78-49f0-9fa6-48ae34e6d930","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"6e9d0f9e-2cbf-41a2-95c4-9bfa6b8e44a8","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to make all the changes. Let me enumerate what needs to be done:\n\n1. **Game Mode: ON** - Registry: HKCU\\Software\\Microsoft\\GameBar - AllowAutoGameMode=1, AutoGameModeEnabled=1\n2. **Game Bar overlay: OFF** - Registry: HKCU\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\GameDVR - AppCaptureEnabled=0; HKCU\\System\\GameConfigStore - GameDVR_Enabled=0\n3. **HAGS: OFF** - Registry: HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\GraphicsDrivers - HwSchMode=1 (0=off, 2=on... wait, let me think. Actually 0=off, 1=on... no. Let me check. HwSchMode values: 0 = off, 1 = on (but not forced), 2 = on (forced). Actually from the earlier check the user has HwSchMode=2 which means on. To disable, set to 0.)\n4. **Power Plan: Ultimate Performance** - powercfg /setactive a1841308-3541-4fab-bc81-f71556f20b4a\n5. **TCP Timestamps: disabled** - netsh int tcp set global timestamps=disabled\n6. **TCP Initial RTO: 300** - netsh int tcp set global initialRto=300\n7. **DNS: set to 223.5.5.5 and 119.29.29.29** - Set-DnsClientServerAddress\n8. **Disable MPO** - Reg: HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Dwm - OverlayTestMode = 5 (DWORD)\n\nLet me write all these in a single PowerShell script.\n\nFor HAGS: HwSchMode values\n- 0 = Disabled\n- 1 = Enabled (user choice)\n- 2 = Enabled (forced by policy)\nThe user has 2, so we need to set to 0.\n\nActually, the proper way to disable HAGS is through the registry:\nHKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\GraphicsDrivers\\HwSchMode = 0\n\nLet me create a comprehensive script.\n\nFor DNS, I need to find the correct interface. The ethernet interface shows as \"以太网\" (index 3 from the netsh output).\n\nLet me write the script carefully.","signature":"6e9d0f9e-2cbf-41a2-95c4-9bfa6b8e44a8"}],"stop_reason":"tool